  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "During the Apollo 11 mission in 1969, astronomers in Germany saw the Moon's Aristarchus crater looking unusually bright, and the crew of Neil Armstrong, Buzz Aldrin and Michael Collins were asked to look and saw it glowing too. The researcher Maaneli Derakhshani tells this to Michels as something he has learned, introducing it with 'apparently', and offers it as part of a case that something unexplained was seen on the Moon."
